   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "15–30 min",
   "title": "Preheat the bath",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Wear gloves. Peel with a vegetable peeler and cut each beet into <b>quarters</b>.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Peel and quarter",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Gloves on: peel with a vegetable peeler.",
      "src": "illustrations/sous-vide-beets/2-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Cut each beet into quarters — fingertips tucked.",
      "src": "illustrations/sous-vide-beets/2-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/sous-vide-beets/2.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~15 min",
   "title": "Peel and quarter",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "500 g (~3 medium)",
     "name_html": "Red beets"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Bag the beets in a <b>single layer</b> with (thyme and garlic optional):<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>olive oil <span class=\"amt\">1 tbsp</span></li><li>salt <span class=\"amt\">½ tsp</span></li><li>vinegar (red wine, balsamic or rice) <span class=\"amt\">1 tsp</span></li><li>thyme <span class=\"amt\">2 sprigs</span></li><li>garlic <span class=\"amt\">1 clove</span></li></ul></li><li>Seal with the vacuum sealer.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Season and vacuum seal",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Seal with the vacuum sealer.",
      "src": "illustrations/sous-vide-beets/3-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/sous-vide-beets/3.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~5 min",
   "title": "Season and vacuum seal",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "Clip the bag to the side and weigh it down — vegetables float, and the bag can puff up as it cooks. <table class=\"mini\"><thead><tr><th>Cut</th><th>Time at 85 °C</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Quarters, medium beets</td><td>about 2 h</td></tr><tr><td>Quarters, large beets</td><td>2–2½ h</td></tr></tbody></table><b>Check:</b> squeeze a piece through the bag with a towel — it should give like a cooked potato. Still firm? Another 30 minutes. A little over is fine; they just get softer.",
   "heat": {
    "label": "85 °C bath",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Cook",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Check: squeeze a piece through the bag with a towel — it should give like a cooked potato.",
      "src": "illustrations/sous-vide-beets/4-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/sous-vide-beets/4.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~2 h",
   "title": "Cook",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>To store, drop the sealed bag into ice water for 15–20 minutes, then refrigerate unopened and use within 5 days.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Chill or serve warm",
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/sous-vide-beets/5.webp",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "15–20 min",
   "title": "Chill or serve warm",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Warm, with:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>butter</li><li>flaky salt</li></ul></li><li>Or cold, with:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>crumbled feta or goat cheese</li><li>walnuts <span class=\"amt\">toasted</span></li><li>dill <span class=\"amt\">chopped</span></li><li>a splash of vinegar</li><li>olive oil</li></ul></li><li>They also go well tossed with the <a href=\"cucumber-sunomono.html\">cucumber pickle</a> dressing.</li></ul>",
